-- title:
--   Geometric fibres of the exceptional components are rational curves
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a package $\mathfrak{X}$ of Deligne–Rapoport model data for $p$, a discrete valuation domain $O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$ together with a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$, and data $H$ satisfying the site hypotheses [`V3Asm.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L267) (finiteness of the node set, existence of oriented crossing charts, the étale-neighbourhood data, injectivity of the node-point assignment, closedness of each node point, and the model hypotheses). Assume further that each of the sections $\xi_j$ lies in the open `X0` of the chart input [`V3Asm.C`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L280), the complement of the finitely many distinguished points. Then for every node $n$ — a point of the fibre product of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$ — and every index $i$ in $\mathrm{Fin}$ of $\mathrm{width}(n) - 1$, where $\mathrm{width}$ is the thickness function of that chart input, there are a curve model $M$ of $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,\kappa$ over $\kappa$ (an integral scheme $M.C$, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$, with function field identified with $\kappa(T)$ compatibly with the base, and with closed points in bijection with the places) and a morphism $e$ from $M.C$ to the pullback along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{to}\kappa$ of the closed immersion of the subscheme cut out by the ideal sheaf $\mathrm{comp}(\mathrm{inr}\,(n,i))$ followed by the structural morphism $\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} O$, such that $e$ is an isomorphism and $e$ followed by the second projection equals $M.\mathrm{toBase}$.
--
--   This is the assertion that each exceptional component produced by resolving a crossing of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ has geometric fibre over the residue field a rational curve, i.e. a smooth proper integral curve with function field $\kappa(T)$, isomorphic to the fibre over $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$ as a $\kappa$-scheme. It is one of the components assembled in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts), which packages the resolved model together with its crossing charts.
-- source:
